  "slug": "discovery-database-1f96",
  "summary": "NAR database-issue updates (canSAR, CIViC, DGIdb, HIPPIE, FusionGDB, PRGdb) land together, pairing expanded curated content with predictive and interoperable tooling.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is mature curated resources expanding coverage while adding predictive or machine-facing layers. canSAR 2026 integrates ML predictors, druggability tools and agentic-AI protein tools. CIViC 2026 introduces Feature entities, Molecular Profiles, AI-guided curation and ClinVar submission. PRGdb 5.0 grows to 874,967 candidate plant resistance proteins with DREM deep-learning prioritization. HIPPIE 3.0 reaches about 1.2M experimentally supported human PPIs and adds negative training sets aimed at interaction prediction. Interoperability and reproducibility form a second axis: DGIdb adds new sources, Python/R clients, Docker images and versioned releases. FusionGDB 3.0 covers 156K fusion genes from RNA-seq and WGS breakpoints and generates personalized fusion protein sequences. CiliaHub provides an expert-curated catalogue of over 2,500 ciliary genes with ClinVar variants. The IDKG preprint takes a graph-integration route, combining 20 infectious-disease sources into a Neo4j graph (4.6M nodes, 26M edges) for graph-based reasoning. Not every resource adds AI components.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-23"
}
